fix-tpmu-name-size: do not let TPMU_NAME pad TPM2B_NAME beyond 66 octets

Classification: spec-deviation bug fix.

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "TPM2B_NAME" (Table: Definition of
TPM2B_NAME Structure)):

  "If size is four, then the Name is a handle. If size is zero, then no Name
  is present. Otherwise, the size shall be the size of a TPM_ALG_ID plus the
  size of the digest produced by the indicated hash algorithm. ...
  name[size]{:sizeof(TPMU_NAME)} BYTE the Name structure"

Specification (TPM 2.0 Library, Part 2, "TPMU_NAME" (Table: Definition of
TPMU_NAME Union)):

  "digest TPMT_HA when the Name is a digest; handle TPM_HANDLE when the Name
  is a handle"

A TPM_HANDLE member pads sizeof(TPMU_NAME) to 68 although the largest
TPMU_NAME is a 66-octet TPMT_HA (Part 2, TPM2B_NAME), so
TPM2B_NAME_Unmarshal() accepted 67- and 68-octet Names that must be rejected
with TPM_RC_SIZE. The handle member becomes a byte array of the same size
and alignment 1.

diff --git a/src/TpmTypes.h b/src/TpmTypes.h
--- a/src/TpmTypes.h
+++ b/src/TpmTypes.h
@@ -1485,7 +1485,11 @@ typedef union {
 /* Table 2:83 - Definition of TPMU_NAME Union  */
 typedef union {
     TPMT_HA                 digest;
-    TPM_HANDLE              handle;
+    // tpm-rs differential testing -- spec deviation fix (NOT determinism):
+    // a TPM_HANDLE member pads sizeof(TPMU_NAME) to 68 although the largest
+    // TPMU_NAME is a 66-octet TPMT_HA (Part 2, TPM2B_NAME), which made
+    // TPM2B_NAME_Unmarshal() accept 67/68-octet Names.
+    BYTE                    handle[sizeof(TPM_HANDLE)];
 } TPMU_NAME;
 /* Table 2:84 - Definition of TPM2B_NAME Structure  */
 typedef union {
